# Who reviews what: GitHub requests a review from the owners of every path a
# pull request touches, and the catch-all below guarantees every path has one.
# Whether a code owner's approval is also *required* is a branch-protection
# setting (`specs/129-github-canonical-migration/` T033), not this file.
#
# The governance section of CONTRIBUTING.md says who decides; this file only
# routes the review request. A later line overrides an earlier one for the paths
# it matches, so narrower rules go below the catch-all.
#
# The owner is the organisation's `maintainers` team. A code owner that is a
# team must be *visible* (a secret team is ignored) and must hold write access
# to this repository, or GitHub reports the line as invalid.

*       @endora-commerce/maintainers
